<title>CANADA: Molson Breweries settles Coors dispute.</title>
<headline>Molson Breweries settles Coors dispute.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian brewer Molson Breweries said on Wednesday that it has settled a dispute with U.S. brewer Adolph Coors Co. in their battle over Molson's licensing rights to Coors' top-selling beers in Canada.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Molson paid Coors C$100 million ($71 million) and will take a C$32.5 million ($23 million) after-tax charge against fiscal 1997 earnings, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Molson said it also agreed to form a new partnership with Coors and Australia's Foster's Brewing Group Ltd. to manage Coors brands in Canada.</p>
</text>
